        "section": "LA Campaign: History & Major Operations",
        "title": "1944 Anarch Free State Revolt & Fall of Don Sebastian",
        "content": "In 1944, Brujah revolutionary Jeremy MacNeil led a ferocious armed rebellion against Los Angeles' tyrannical Camarilla Prince, Don Sebastian Juan Dominguez, after Sebastian ordered MacNeil beaten for minor insolence. The ensuing popular uprising purged the Camarilla court from the basin, drove Sebastian to his Final Death, and permanently established Los Angeles as the global capital of the Anarch Free State.",
